{"id": "EUVD-2026-103836", "enisaUuid": "3b9ba7f8-5443-3868-b35b-74c5e9d14a6f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntty: abort break signalling on hangup\n\nThe break ioctls can race with hangup and end up calling into a tty\ndriver for a device that is already gone or powered down.\n\nDrivers must handle this race, but TCSBRK and TCSBRKP should still be\naborted to avoid calling back into the driver after a user-controlled\ntimeout (possibly even after the tty has been reopened).\n\nNote that drivers should disable any break state on shutdown so just\nreturn on hangup (calling break_ctl() again is racy and will most likely\nfail for drivers handling the race).", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c9c9367351a461d62e5c0a39bffdcfbb40f068b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3bc82999fb85cecc7eb6ec1755ee7d698aa1e783", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94af6cd832e9b4ce39a8fb59144a8f09ab56fd35", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8ccd3b2013daaf77b98f8a6724fcf4d2c5c52d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/845a2737e0f5ffe5ca8d38de556012b0c9472cdd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98751", "GHSA-cg92-2wfv-ppg3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01b49191-818c-3014-b9ef-93a2be50bc87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f34d7a5b7010b82fe97da95496b9971435530062 <6c9c9367351a461d62e5c0a39bffdcfbb40f068b"}, {"id": "156f5338-99f3-3f33-bb99-0ed3e62450e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.26"}, {"id": "31fe751e-6801-3d4d-9088-de02162a160c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "4d8e7f92-11f0-357d-82e7-e27ae0ff43f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f34d7a5b7010b82fe97da95496b9971435530062 <3bc82999fb85cecc7eb6ec1755ee7d698aa1e783"}, {"id": "7cc5c25f-c9bd-3dfa-b4b9-65028567731f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "84af1048-ad09-3901-b3ec-b07902ff6947", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f34d7a5b7010b82fe97da95496b9971435530062 <845a2737e0f5ffe5ca8d38de556012b0c9472cdd"}, {"id": "8556e59e-cddb-34b1-b3fb-8c9df4ac3cf3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9b34a284-b4b5-3d18-b12b-a6ae081fe5dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "a8baa0ad-44d6-3f16-a8f3-5e5194970aa6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f34d7a5b7010b82fe97da95496b9971435530062 <c8ccd3b2013daaf77b98f8a6724fcf4d2c5c52d6"}, {"id": "b089a1ef-dd83-34f3-b043-189a2863b5ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b4ca9107-e556-33f2-aa22-98dff2bfe83c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f34d7a5b7010b82fe97da95496b9971435530062 <94af6cd832e9b4ce39a8fb59144a8f09ab56fd35"}, {"id": "fdb3f608-c9c9-3381-a798-dee32eee153f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "db846eca-750f-321b-a5f2-0e54989d2771", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}